{"phases":32,"frame":"Pelvis frame, units = leg length (thigh+shin = 1). Origin = mid-hip. +x = skier's RIGHT (left hip -> right hip), +y = up the spine (mid-hip -> mid-shoulder, orthogonalised to x), +z = x cross y = BACKWARD (forward = -z). The cycle is ONE RIGHT TURN: phase 0 = edge change into the right turn, ~0.5 = apex, phase 1 = next edge change. Play the next (left) turn by mirroring: x -> -x and swap l_/r_; negate inclination, twist, feetYaw, hipLateral. The pair is periodic and Fourier-smoothed, so phase 31 -> mirrored phase 0 is continuous.","inclination":[0.063,0.1251,0.1816,0.2313,0.2736,0.3085,0.3364,0.358,0.3746,0.3875,0.3979,0.4073,0.4166,0.4265,0.4375,0.4493,0.4614,0.4727,0.4821,0.4879,0.4887,0.483,0.4694,0.4472,0.4158,0.3753,0.3261,0.2695,0.207,0.1403,0.0717,0.0032],"inclination_note":"radians, lean of the line mid-ankle -> mid-hip from gravity vertical, sideways relative to the pelvis; + = hips to the skier's right of the feet (inside of a right turn)","hipHeight":[0.8053,0.7892,0.7713,0.7527,0.7338,0.715,0.6959,0.6762,0.6554,0.6334,0.6101,0.5862,0.5628,0.5412,0.5232,0.5107,0.5053,0.5083,0.5203,0.5412,0.57,0.6051,0.6442,0.6847,0.7237,0.7589,0.788,0.8097,0.8232,0.8286,0.8265,0.8183],"hipHeight_note":"vertical height of mid-hip above mid-ankle / leg length (1 = standing straight over the feet)","hipLateral":[0.0362,0.09,0.1387,0.1808,0.2151,0.241,0.2587,0.2689,0.2726,0.2716,0.2675,0.2624,0.2579,0.2554,0.2562,0.2607,0.2688,0.2801,0.2934,0.3071,0.3194,0.3285,0.3323,0.3292,0.318,0.2979,0.2687,0.2307,0.1851,0.1335,0.0779,0.0205],"hipFore":[-0.3196,-0.3223,-0.3149,-0.2984,-0.2755,-0.2495,-0.2245,-0.204,-0.1912,-0.1877,-0.1941,-0.2091,-0.2304,-0.2544,-0.2773,-0.2956,-0.3063,-0.3076,-0.2993,-0.2827,-0.2601,-0.2351,-0.2116,-0.1931,-0.1827,-0.1821,-0.1914,-0.2096,-0.2338,-0.2608,-0.2864,-0.307],"hipOffset_note":"horizontal offset of mid-hip from mid-ankle / leg length: lateral (+ = right) and fore (+ = forward)","twist":[-0.0254,-0.0942,-0.1501,-0.192,-0.219